{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "JOB",
  "chapter": 42,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "JOB.42.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.42.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then Job answered the LORD, and said,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.42.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.42.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I know that thou canst do every ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "thing",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " no thought can be withheld from thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.42.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.42.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " he that hideth counsel without knowledge? therefore have I uttered that which I understood not; things too wonderful for me, which I knew not.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.42.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.42.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Hear, I beseech thee, and I will speak: I will ask of thee, and declare thou to me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.42.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.42.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I have heard of thee by the hearing of the ear: but now my eye seeth thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.42.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.42.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Wherefore I abhor ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "myself",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and repent in dust and ashes.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.42.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.42.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And it was ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "so",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", that after the LORD had spoken these words to Job, the LORD said to Eliphaz the Temanite, My wrath is kindled against thee, and against thy two friends: for ye have not spoken of me ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "the thing that is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " right, as my servant Job ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "hath",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.42.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.42.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore take to you now seven bullocks and seven rams, and go to my servant Job, and offer for yourselves a burnt-offering; and my servant Job shall pray for you: for him will I accept: lest I deal with you ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "after your",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " folly, in that ye have not spoken of me ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "the thing which is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " right, like my servant Job.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.42.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.42.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So Eliphaz the Temanite and Bildad the Shuhite ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " Zophar the Naamathite went, and did according as the LORD commanded them: the LORD also accepted Job.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.42.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.42.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the LORD turned the captivity of Job, when he prayed for his friends: also the LORD gave Job twice as much as he had before.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.42.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.42.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then came there to him all his brethren, and all his sisters, and all they that had been of his acquaintance before, and ate bread with him in his house: and they condoled with him, and comforted him over all the evil that the LORD had brought upon him: every man also gave him a piece of money, and every one an ear-ring of gold.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.42.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.42.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So the LORD blessed the latter end of Job more than his beginning: for he had fourteen thousand sheep, and six thousand camels, and a thousand yoke of oxen, and a thousand she asses.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.42.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.42.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He had also seven sons, and three daughters.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.42.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.42.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he called the name of the first, Jemima; and the name of the second, Kezia; and the name of the third, Keren-happuch.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.42.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.42.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And in all the land were no women found ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "so",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " fair as the daughters of Job: and their father gave them inheritance among their brethren.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.42.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.42.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "After this Job lived a hundred and forty years, and saw his sons, and his sons' sons, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " four generations.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.42.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.42.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So Job died, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "being",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " old and full of days.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
